#: ../../src/design.rst:31
msgid "Handles and requests"
msgstr "句柄与请求"

#: ../../src/design.rst:33
msgid ""
"libuv provides users with 2 abstractions to work with, in combination "
"with the event loop: handles and requests."
msgstr ""
"libuv 为用户提供了 2 种可与事件循环配合使用的抽象：句柄和请求。"

#: ../../src/design.rst:36
msgid ""
"Handles represent long-lived objects capable of performing certain "
"operations while active. Some examples:"
msgstr ""
"句柄代表长生命周期的对象，在活动期间能够执行某些操作。示例如下："

#: ../../src/design.rst:38
msgid ""
"A prepare handle gets its callback called once every loop iteration when "
"active."
msgstr ""
"prepare 句柄在活动状态下，每轮循环迭代其回调都会被调用一次。"

#: ../../src/design.rst:39
msgid ""
"A TCP server handle that gets its connection callback called every time "
"there is a new connection."
msgstr ""
"TCP 服务器句柄，每当出现新连接时，其连接回调都会被调用。"

#: ../../src/design.rst:41
msgid ""
"Requests represent (typically) short-lived operations. These operations "
"can be performed over a handle: write requests are used to write data on "
"a handle; or standalone: getaddrinfo requests don't need a handle they "
"run directly on the loop."
msgstr ""
"请求代表（通常）短生命周期的操作。这些操作可以在句柄之上执行：写请求用于"
"向句柄写入数据；也可以独立执行：getaddrinfo 请求不需要句柄，直接在事件循"
"环上运行。"

#: ../../src/design.rst:45
msgid "Guidelines for dealing with handles and requests:"
msgstr "处理句柄与请求的准则："

#: ../../src/design.rst:47
msgid ""
"If `uv_foo_init()` succeeds in initializing the handle, you must call "
":c:func:`uv_close`. If the handle's init function errors, you don't need "
"to do anything."
msgstr ""
"如果 `uv_foo_init()` 成功初始化了句柄，就必须调用 :c:func:`uv_close`。"
"如果句柄的 init 函数出错，则无需做任何事情。"

#: ../../src/design.rst:51
msgid ""
"Only handles are closed, not requests. For example, :c:type:`uv_tcp_t` is"
" a handle, :c:type:`uv_write_t` is a request."
msgstr ""
"只有句柄会被关闭，请求则不会。例如，:c:type:`uv_tcp_t` 是句柄，"
":c:type:`uv_write_t` 是请求。"

#: ../../src/design.rst:54
msgid ""
"The handle's memory can only be reclaimed or reused from inside the "
":c:type:`uv_close_cb` or afterwards, not before."
msgstr ""
"句柄的内存只能在 :c:type:`uv_close_cb` 内部或之后被回收或复用，在此之前"
"不行。"

#: ../../src/design.rst:57
msgid ""
"Most handles have init + start/stop functions; some handles don't. "
"Example: :c:type:`uv_tcp_t` vs. :c:type:`uv_process_t`; "
":c:func:`uv_spawn` combines handle initialization and process start into "
"one."
msgstr ""
"大多数句柄都有 init + start/stop 函数；有些句柄则没有。例如："
":c:type:`uv_tcp_t` 与 :c:type:`uv_process_t` 的对比；:c:func:`uv_spawn`"
" 将句柄初始化和进程启动合而为一。"

#: ../../src/design.rst:61
msgid ""
"Requests are closed automatically when they complete, or when they are "
"cancelled with :c:func:`uv_cancel`."
msgstr ""
"请求会在完成时自动关闭，或在通过 :c:func:`uv_cancel` 被取消时自动关闭。"

#: ../../src/design.rst:64
msgid ""
"No additional cleanup is needed except for :c:type:`uv_fs_t` and "
":c:type:`uv_getaddrinfo_t` requests. For :c:type:`uv_fs_t`, call "
":c:func:`uv_fs_req_cleanup` once you are done with it; for "
":c:type:`uv_getaddrinfo_t`, that's :c:func:`uv_freeaddrinfo`."
msgstr ""
"除 :c:type:`uv_fs_t` 和 :c:type:`uv_getaddrinfo_t` 请求外，无需额外的清"
"理。对于 :c:type:`uv_fs_t`，用完后调用 :c:func:`uv_fs_req_cleanup`；对"
"于 :c:type:`uv_getaddrinfo_t`，则调用 :c:func:`uv_freeaddrinfo`。"

#: ../../src/design.rst:69
msgid ""
"The request's memory can only be reclaimed or reused from that point "
"onward."
msgstr ""
"请求的内存只能从那一刻起被回收或复用。"

#: ../../src/design.rst:72
msgid "The I/O loop"
msgstr "I/O 循环"

#: ../../src/design.rst:74
msgid ""
"The I/O (or event) loop is the central part of libuv. It establishes the "
"content for all I/O operations, and it's meant to be tied to a single "
"thread. One can run multiple event loops as long as each runs in a "
"different thread. The libuv event loop (or any other API involving the "
"loop or handles, for that matter) **is not thread-safe** except where "
"stated otherwise."
msgstr ""
"I/O（即事件）循环是 libuv 的核心部分。它为所有 I/O 操作建立了上下文，并且"
"应当绑定到单个线程。可以运行多个事件循环，只要各自运行在不同的线程中。"
"libuv 事件循环（就此而言，还包括任何涉及循环或句柄的其他 API）"
"**不是线程安全的**，除非另有说明。"

#: ../../src/design.rst:79
msgid ""
"The event loop follows the rather usual single threaded asynchronous I/O "
"approach: all (network) I/O is performed on non-blocking sockets which "
"are polled using the best mechanism available on the given platform: "
"epoll on Linux, kqueue on OSX and other BSDs, event ports on SunOS and "
"IOCP on Windows. As part of a loop iteration the loop will block waiting "
"for I/O activity on sockets which have been added to the poller and "
"callbacks will be fired indicating socket conditions (readable, writable "
"hangup) so handles can read, write or perform the desired I/O operation."
msgstr ""
"事件循环采用相当常见的单线程异步 I/O 方式：所有（网络）I/O 都在非阻塞套接"
"字上进行，并使用给定平台上可用的最佳机制轮询这些套接字：Linux 上是"
" epoll，OSX 及其他 BSD 上是 kqueue，SunOS 上是 event ports，Windows 上是"
" IOCP。作为循环迭代的一部分，循环会阻塞等待已加入轮询器的套接字上的 I/O 活"
"动，并触发回调来指示套接字状态（可读、可写、挂断），使句柄能够读取、写入"
"或执行所需的 I/O 操作。"

#: ../../src/design.rst:86
msgid ""
"In order to better understand how the event loop operates, the following "
"diagram illustrates all stages of a loop iteration:"
msgstr ""
"为了更好地理解事件循环是如何运作的，下图展示了一轮循环迭代的全部阶段："

#: ../../src/design.rst:-1
msgid "Picture of libuv loop iteration"
msgstr "libuv 循环迭代示意图"

#: ../../src/design.rst:100
msgid "The loop concept of 'now' is initially set."
msgstr "循环的“now”概念被初始设定。"

#: ../../src/design.rst:102
msgid ""
"Due timers are run if the loop was run with ``UV_RUN_DEFAULT``. All "
"active timers scheduled for a time before the loop's concept of *now* get"
" their callbacks called."
msgstr ""
"如果循环以 ``UV_RUN_DEFAULT`` 模式运行，到期的定时器就会被执行。所有计划"
"时间早于循环的 *now* 概念的活动定时器，其回调都会被调用。"

#: ../../src/design.rst:105
msgid ""
"If the loop is *alive*  an iteration is started, otherwise the loop will "
"exit immediately. So, when is a loop considered to be *alive*? If a loop "
"has active and ref'd handles, active requests or closing handles it's "
"considered to be *alive*."
msgstr ""
"如果循环 *存活*，就会开始一轮迭代，否则循环将立即退出。那么，何时认为循环"
" *存活*？如果循环有活动且被引用的句柄、活动的请求或正在关闭的句柄，就认为"
"它 *存活*。"

#: ../../src/design.rst:109
msgid ""
"Pending callbacks are called. All I/O callbacks are called right after "
"polling for I/O, for the most part. There are cases, however, in which "
"calling such a callback is deferred for the next loop iteration. If the "
"previous iteration deferred any I/O callback it will be run at this "
"point."
msgstr ""
"挂起的回调会被调用。大体上，所有 I/O 回调都会在轮询 I/O 之后立即被调用。"
"但也有一些情况，这类回调的调用会被推迟到下一轮循环迭代。如果上一轮迭代推"
"迟了任何 I/O 回调，它就会在此刻被执行。"

#: ../../src/design.rst:113
msgid ""
"Idle handle callbacks are called. Despite the unfortunate name, idle "
"handles are run on every loop iteration, if they are active."
msgstr ""
"Idle 句柄的回调会被调用。尽管这个名字起得不太恰当，但只要处于活动状态，"
"idle 句柄在每轮循环迭代中都会运行。"

#: ../../src/design.rst:116
msgid ""
"Prepare handle callbacks are called. Prepare handles get their callbacks "
"called right before the loop will block for I/O."
msgstr ""
"Prepare 句柄的回调会被调用。Prepare 句柄的回调恰好在循环阻塞等待 I/O 之"
"前被调用。"

#: ../../src/design.rst:119
msgid ""
"Poll timeout is calculated. Before blocking for I/O the loop calculates "
"for how long it should block. These are the rules when calculating the "
"timeout:"
msgstr ""
"计算轮询超时。在阻塞等待 I/O 之前，循环会计算应该阻塞多长时间。以下是计"
"算超时时使用的规则："

#: ../../src/design.rst:122
msgid "If the loop was run with the ``UV_RUN_NOWAIT`` flag, the timeout is 0."
msgstr "如果循环以 ``UV_RUN_NOWAIT`` 标志运行，则超时为 0。"

#: ../../src/design.rst:123
msgid ""
"If the loop is going to be stopped (:c:func:`uv_stop` was called), the "
"timeout is 0."
msgstr ""
"如果循环即将停止（已调用 :c:func:`uv_stop`），则超时为 0。"

#: ../../src/design.rst:124
msgid "If there are no active handles or requests, the timeout is 0."
msgstr "如果没有活动的句柄或请求，则超时为 0。"

#: ../../src/design.rst:125
msgid "If there are any idle handles active, the timeout is 0."
msgstr "如果有任何处于活动状态的 idle 句柄，则超时为 0。"

#: ../../src/design.rst:126
msgid "If there are any handles pending to be closed, the timeout is 0."
msgstr "如果有任何句柄等待关闭，则超时为 0。"

#: ../../src/design.rst:127
msgid ""
"If none of the above cases matches, the timeout of the closest timer is "
"taken, or if there are no active timers, infinity."
msgstr ""
"如果以上情况都不匹配，则取最近一个定时器的超时；如果没有活动的定时器，则"
"为无穷大。"

#: ../../src/design.rst:130
msgid ""
"The loop blocks for I/O. At this point the loop will block for I/O for "
"the duration calculated in the previous step. All I/O related handles "
"that were monitoring a given file descriptor for a read or write "
"operation get their callbacks called at this point."
msgstr ""
"循环阻塞等待 I/O。此时，循环会按上一步计算出的时长阻塞等待 I/O。所有正在"
"监视某个文件描述符的读或写操作的 I/O 相关句柄，其回调都会在此刻被调用。"

#: ../../src/design.rst:134
msgid ""
"Check handle callbacks are called. Check handles get their callbacks "
"called right after the loop has blocked for I/O. Check handles are "
"essentially the counterpart of prepare handles."
msgstr ""
"Check 句柄的回调会被调用。Check 句柄的回调会在循环阻塞等待 I/O 之后立即"
"被调用。Check 句柄本质上是 prepare 句柄的对应物。"

#: ../../src/design.rst:137
msgid ""
"Close callbacks are called. If a handle was closed by calling "
":c:func:`uv_close` it will get the close callback called."
msgstr ""
"关闭回调会被调用。如果句柄是通过调用 :c:func:`uv_close` 被关闭的，其关闭"
"回调就会被调用。"

#: ../../src/design.rst:140
msgid "The loop concept of 'now' is updated."
msgstr "循环的“now”概念被更新。"

#: ../../src/design.rst:142
msgid ""
"Due timers are run. Note that 'now' is not updated again until the next "
"loop iteration. So if a timer became due while other timers were being "
"processed, it won't be run until the following event loop iteration."
msgstr ""
"到期的定时器会被执行。注意，在下一轮循环迭代之前，“now”不会再次更新。因"
"此，如果某个定时器在其他定时器被处理期间到期，它要到下一次事件循环迭代才"
"会运行。"

#: ../../src/design.rst:146
msgid ""
"Iteration ends. If the loop was run with ``UV_RUN_NOWAIT`` or "
"``UV_RUN_ONCE`` modes the iteration ends and :c:func:`uv_run` will "
"return. If the loop was run with ``UV_RUN_DEFAULT`` it will continue from"
" the start if it's still *alive*, otherwise it will also end."
msgstr ""
"迭代结束。如果循环以 ``UV_RUN_NOWAIT`` 或 ``UV_RUN_ONCE`` 模式运行，迭代"
"结束，:c:func:`uv_run` 将返回。如果循环以 ``UV_RUN_DEFAULT`` 模式运行，"
"只要它仍然 *存活*，就会从头开始继续，否则也会结束。"

#: ../../src/design.rst:152
msgid ""
"libuv uses a thread pool to make asynchronous file I/O operations "
"possible, but network I/O is **always** performed in a single thread, "
"each loop's thread."
msgstr ""
"libuv 使用线程池使异步文件 I/O 操作成为可能，但网络 I/O **始终** 在单个线"
"程中执行，即每个循环各自的线程。"

#: ../../src/design.rst:156
msgid ""
"While the polling mechanism is different, libuv makes the execution model"
" consistent across Unix systems and Windows."
msgstr ""
"尽管轮询机制各不相同，libuv 使执行模型在 Unix 系统和 Windows 上保持一致。"

#: ../../src/design.rst:161
msgid "File I/O"
msgstr "文件 I/O"

#: ../../src/design.rst:163
msgid ""
"Unlike network I/O, there are no platform-specific file I/O primitives "
"libuv could rely on, so the current approach is to run blocking file I/O "
"operations in a thread pool."
msgstr ""
"与网络 I/O 不同，并不存在 libuv 可以依赖的平台特定的文件 I/O 原语，因此目"
"前的做法是在线程池中运行阻塞式文件 I/O 操作。"

#: ../../src/design.rst:166
msgid ""
"For a thorough explanation of the cross-platform file I/O landscape, "
"check out `this post <https://blog.libtorrent.org/2012/10/asynchronous-"
"disk-io/>`_."
msgstr ""
"关于跨平台文件 I/O 全貌的详尽阐述，请参阅 `这篇文章"
" <https://blog.libtorrent.org/2012/10/asynchronous-disk-io/>`_。"

#: ../../src/design.rst:169
msgid ""
"libuv currently uses a global thread pool on which all loops can queue "
"work. 3 types of operations are currently run on this pool:"
msgstr ""
"libuv 目前使用一个全局线程池，所有循环都可以在其中排队工作。目前在这个线"
"程池上运行的有 3 类操作："

#: ../../src/design.rst:172
msgid "File system operations"
msgstr "文件系统操作"

#: ../../src/design.rst:173
msgid "DNS functions (getaddrinfo and getnameinfo)"
msgstr "DNS 函数（getaddrinfo 和 getnameinfo）"

#: ../../src/design.rst:174
msgid "User specified code via :c:func:`uv_queue_work`"
msgstr "通过 :c:func:`uv_queue_work` 指定的用户代码"

#: ../../src/design.rst:177
msgid ""
"See the :c:ref:`threadpool` section for more details, but keep in mind "
"the thread pool size is quite limited."
msgstr ""
"详情请参阅 :c:ref:`threadpool` 一节，但请记住线程池的大小相当有限。"

